(7464486, 1183876, 114285, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by wbanning:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by tvsometime:</b></div><hr/><i> This is visually perplexing as is but reversing the upside down perspective yields a beautifully executed image, bird and all. I''ld like to give an 8 but can''t because it''s uncomfortable to keep turning my monitor upside down. So just a 6. Sorry I don''t appreciate your aesthetic but maybe with time... </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Ok, Tom, if you''re turning the monitor upside down, shouldn''t that be a 9 not a 6?<br/> <br/>Nicely done, Neat! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/> Like!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2016-07-15 04:44:15.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by wbanning: Originally posted by tvsometime: This is visually perplexing as is but reversing the upside down perspective yields a beautifully executed image, bird and all. I''ld like to give an 8 but can''t because it''s uncomfortable to keep turning my monitor upside down. So just a 6. Sorry I don''t appreciate your aesthetic but maybe with time...   Ok, Tom, if you''re turning the monitor upside down, shouldn''t that be a 9 not a 6? Nicely done, Neat!    Like!', '2016-07-15 02:42:57.000000', '2016-07-15 05:44:15.000000', 0),
